      "summary": "build_01: Add the root CMake build definition for the bounded Ascend910B3 Roll operator draft, wired to the official CANNBot package/subdirectory build pattern.; build_02: Stage 2/17 adds an isolated build script for the Roll operator package with optional UT/ST/example entrypoints and no implicit installation.; build_03: Added the isolated op_host CMake configuration for the Roll operator, wiring schema, infer-shape, Ascend910B tiling, ACLNN API sources, and package libraries.; build_04: Adds the isolated Roll kernel CMake for Ascend910B3/arch22 with explicit unsupported-SoC rejection.; host_01: Added complete Roll host operator definition for float32 tensor input, shift/axis scalar attributes, and Ascend910B3 configuration.; host_02: Added Roll infer-shape host implementation copying the input tensor shape to the single output.; host_03: Stage 7/17 host_03: complete arch22 host tiling for Roll (float32 segment-copy contract, explicit rejection of unsupported dtype/dynamic/axis cases, workspace + blockdim + TilingData setup).; kernel_01: Stage 8/17 — adds `op_kernel/roll_arch22.cpp`: self-contained Ascend910B (arch22) kernel entry for `Roll` (float32), with tiling-data contract, Init -> CopyIn -> Compute -> CopyOut structure, and exact cyclic-rotation indexing (dst[p] = src[(p - shiftOffset) mod rowLen]) covering axis=None and any valid axis.; kernel_02: Stage 9/17 kernel_02: complete arch22 Roll kernel class header (float32, Init/CopyIn/Compute/CopyOut, cyclic-shift segment decomposition) for op_kernel/arch22/roll.h; kernel_03: Stage 10 kernel_03 defines the shared RollTilingData layout for arch22 host tiling and kernel use.; kernel_04: Stage 11 kernel_04 adds the arch22 Roll tiling-key declaration for float32-only template selection.; api_01: Added the complete two-stage ACLNN L2 header for Roll, preserving NumPy argument order and explicit output tensor semantics.; api_02: Implemented ACLNN L2 Roll workspace/execute entry with float32-only validation and bounded explicit-axis support.; api_03: Declared the complete L0 ACLNN interface for Roll with NumPy-compatible shift/axis ordering and executor-managed output allocation.; api_04: Implemented the Roll ACLNN L0 API with float32/platform checks, shape inference, output allocation, and explicit launcher error handling.; test_adapter_01: Stage 16/17 test_adapter_01: add roll adapter tests with NumPy oracle coverage and guarded public asnumpy.roll checks.; test_adapter_02: Generated the roll AsNumpy adapter manifest with explicit symbol mapping, bounded float32 profile, rejections, and exact numerical policy.",
